      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1297739305,
      "text": "Asperugo procumbens, known as German madwort, is the single species in the monotypic plant genus Asperugo. This plant is native to Europe and temperate parts of Asia but has been introduced elsewhere by humans."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Asperugo",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asperugo",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 135211669,
      "text": "Asperugo es un género de plantas con flores perteneciente a la familia Boraginaceae. Comprende 8 especies descritas y de estas, solo una aceptada. Su única especie: Asperugo procumbens, se distribuye por el Norte de África y Eurasia."
    }
